#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# enclose

#% text
# `enclose(e)` gives the value of `e`, or the failure that a `confirm` inside it threw. `enclose(e, f)` gives `f` of that failure; `enclose(e, f, tag)` catches only the throws of `confirm(x, info, tag)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
enclose(confirm(2) + 3)
#% output
#= 5

#% cell
enclose(confirm(missing()) + 3)
#% output
#! failure(confirmation_failed, missing())

#% cell
enclose(confirm(missing()) + 3, v => "no value")
#% output
#! failure(confirmation_failed, missing())

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `confirm`, `catch`, `check`
